"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 4.5 and an ISUP grade group 2 pathology from the prostatectomy specimen. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins, no seminal vesicle invasion, and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The pathological stage was pT2, with no documented extraprostatic extension. A countervailing finding is the lack of nodal sampling; thus, the status remains unknown, widening uncertainty regarding regional spread. Furthermore, there is a discrepancy between the biopsy findings (right transition zone) and the prostatectomy specimen analysis, though both report ISUP grade group 2. The absence of documented lymph node removal prevents definitive staging for this aspect. Prognostic assessment would be significantly revised by obtaining postoperative PSA levels and tracking their subsequent trajectory over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 84.76 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.86–118.66 months; its coverage has not been validated."
